From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 18:22:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] RISC OS: a start-up and drawing trace (TORCS$Trace), and
 TORCS$NoSound

For finding where TORCS stops (riscos6test1 mixed locked up under RISC OS
on Linux with RISC3D, straight after the "Visual Properties Report").

tgf/riscostrace.cpp, off unless TORCS$Trace is set:
- riscosTrace() writes a line to the log with the time since start;
- riscosTraceStage() notes where the main thread is, without writing;
- riscosTraceFrame() counts frames (written: the first five, then every
  hundredth);
- a watchdog thread writes the last stage if the main thread makes no
  progress for 5 s, then every 10 s. If the log just stops, the main
  thread is stuck where even the thread switcher can't run (in a SWI).
Marked: directories, GfScrInit, glutCreateWindow, the GL strings,
ssgInit, GfInitClient, the main menu, the splash image, the menu music,
glutMainLoop, each swap in the splash and GfuiDisplay, the splash
closing, menu screen changes, the menu music buffer, race sound.

riscosNoSound() (TORCS$NoSound set): no menu music and no race sound, so
OpenAL isn't started.
